WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.415
Lesson 0.5.

00:00:02.415 --> 00:00:04.710
Setting up your wallet and backing it up.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.145
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:07.145 --> 00:00:09.755
to install a wallet safely, back up the seed

00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:12.364
phrase correctly, and prove the backup works.

00:00:13.664 --> 00:00:14.954
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.954 --> 00:00:16.639
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:19.354
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:19.354 --> 00:00:20.879
Then, your checklist.

00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:23.041
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:24.341 --> 00:00:27.187
Two kinds of wallet: Safe install: Prove the

00:00:27.187 --> 00:00:29.907
backup works (do this now, with nothing in

00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:32.500
the wallet): remove the wallet (or use a

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.611
second device), choose "restore/import", enter your written seed

00:00:36.611 --> 00:00:39.631
phrase, and check the same address appears.

00:00:39.631 --> 00:00:44.279
First, Software wallet (browser extension or phone app, e.g.

00:00:44.279 --> 00:00:49.836
MetaMask, Rabby): free, convenient; keys live on your computer/phone.

00:00:49.836 --> 00:00:53.335
Next, Hardware wallet (a small device, e.g. Ledger,

00:00:53.335 --> 00:00:56.835
Trezor): keys stay on the device; every transaction

00:00:56.835 --> 00:00:59.221
must be approved on its screen.

00:00:59.221 --> 00:01:01.213
Recommended once you hold more than

00:01:01.213 --> 00:01:02.785
you'd be upset to lose.

00:01:02.785 --> 00:01:07.210
Buy only from the manufacturer's official website, never second-hand.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.401
Then, Get the wallet from the official

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:11.761
website (type the address yourself or use

00:01:11.761 --> 00:01:13.915
the link from the official site).

00:01:13.915 --> 00:01:16.166
Fake wallet apps and sponsored search

00:01:16.166 --> 00:01:17.770
ads are a common scam.

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:19.735
Also, Create a new wallet.

00:01:19.735 --> 00:01:22.187
Never use a seed phrase someone else gave

00:01:22.187 --> 00:01:24.705
you or that came pre-printed in a box.

00:01:24.705 --> 00:01:26.527
On top of that, Write the seed

00:01:26.527 --> 00:01:28.526
phrase on paper (or stamp it into

00:01:28.526 --> 00:01:30.525
metal), in order, spelled exactly.

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.686
And Store it somewhere private and

00:01:33.686 --> 00:01:35.315
safe from fire and water.

00:01:35.315 --> 00:01:37.325
For larger amounts, keep a second

00:01:37.325 --> 00:01:39.280
copy in a separate location.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.339
And finally, never store it in photos, email,

00:01:42.339 --> 00:01:45.398
notes apps, cloud drives or password managers.

00:01:46.698 --> 00:01:48.249
Let's look at the diagram:

00:01:48.249 --> 00:01:50.043
Seed phrase: do and don't.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.603
Take a moment with it.

00:01:51.603 --> 00:01:54.013
It's everything we've just said, in one picture.

00:01:55.313 --> 00:01:57.828
Let's work an example, step by

00:01:57.828 --> 00:02:01.381
step. Sam installs Rabby from its official site, writes

00:02:01.381 --> 00:02:04.172
12 words on the card in his hardware wallet

00:02:04.172 --> 00:02:06.837
box (the card is blank, as it should be),

00:02:06.837 --> 00:02:10.263
restores on his laptop, sees the same address 0x4b…e1,

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:13.258
and only then sends money to it.

00:02:14.558 --> 00:02:16.018
Here's your checklist.

00:02:16.018 --> 00:02:17.553
Do it now, for real.

00:02:17.553 --> 00:02:20.618
First, Wallet installed from the official website.

00:02:20.618 --> 00:02:22.738
Next, New seed phrase written on

00:02:22.738 --> 00:02:25.093
paper (or metal), never digital.

00:02:25.093 --> 00:02:28.348
Then, Restore test done: same address appears.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:31.058
And finally, Hardware wallet planned for larger

00:02:31.058 --> 00:02:33.373
amounts (bought from the maker directly).

00:02:34.673 --> 00:02:35.883
Question 1.

00:02:35.883 --> 00:02:37.874
A wallet box contains a card

00:02:37.874 --> 00:02:40.233
with 24 words already printed.

00:02:40.233 --> 00:02:41.083
What do you do?

00:02:45.503 --> 00:02:47.298
The answer: Don't use it.

00:02:47.298 --> 00:02:48.468
It's a scam.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:51.796
Genuine devices generate your seed phrase themselves.

00:02:53.096 --> 00:02:54.341
Question 2.

00:02:54.341 --> 00:02:56.486
Why test the restore before depositing?

00:03:00.906 --> 00:03:03.134
The answer: To prove your written backup

00:03:03.134 --> 00:03:05.091
is correct while nothing is at risk.

00:03:06.391 --> 00:03:07.661
Question 3.

00:03:07.661 --> 00:03:09.437
Is a cloud-drive photo of your

00:03:09.437 --> 00:03:10.926
seed phrase a safe backup?

00:03:15.346 --> 00:03:17.277
The answer: No. Anyone who gets

00:03:17.277 --> 00:03:19.571
into that account can take everything.

00:03:20.871 --> 00:03:22.116
Let's recap.

00:03:22.116 --> 00:03:24.816
Software wallet (browser extension or

00:03:24.816 --> 00:03:27.461
phone app, e.g. MetaMask, Rabby).

00:03:27.461 --> 00:03:31.406
Hardware wallet (a small device, e.g. Ledger, Trezor).

00:03:31.406 --> 00:03:33.621
Get the wallet from the official website

00:03:33.621 --> 00:03:35.674
(type the address yourself or use the

00:03:35.674 --> 00:03:37.541
link from the official site).

00:03:37.541 --> 00:03:39.541
Create a new wallet: Never use a

00:03:39.541 --> 00:03:41.783
seed phrase someone else gave you or

00:03:41.783 --> 00:03:43.661
that came pre-printed in a box.

00:03:44.961 --> 00:03:47.476
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:47.476 --> 00:03:49.959
Next up, Lesson 0.6: Networks,

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:52.201
gas and your first transfer.
